# Apache config for Hostinger. Everything in public/ is copied into out/, and
# out/ is what gets force-pushed to the deploy branch - so this file ships.
#
# REDIRECTS LIVE HERE, NOT IN next.config.js. This site is output: 'export'
# (static), and Next does not support redirects() in that mode: the block would
# sit there looking correct and do nothing at all. CUE learnt this the same way.

# Two pages were retired in Sep 2026 (Wayan):
#   /villas      the listing of two villas - the menu now opens the two villa
#                pages directly, and the homepage band took over the "see both"
#                job, which is where this points.
#   /experiences four illustrative category cards nobody could book - the real
#                tours are on the sister site, and the homepage band links out.
#
# RedirectMatch WITH ANCHORS, never plain `Redirect`: mod_alias's Redirect
# matches a path PREFIX, so `Redirect 301 /villas /` would also catch
# /villas/cahyana-house/ and send both live villa pages to the homepage.
# ^/villas/?$ matches the retired page and nothing below it.
RedirectMatch 301 ^/villas/?$ /#villas
RedirectMatch 301 ^/experiences/?$ /
